.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
node_modules/
.env

# Generated artefacts. These must stay in step with gate.yaml's denylist —
# `pf check` fails if git is tracking anything the gate calls generated. They
# drifted once: the patterns here were written without `**/`, which anchors them
# to the repo root, so `groups/*/projects/*/kg/graph.duckdb` was never ignored
# and 1,622 regenerable files ended up committed.
**/target/
# `target-base/` is where the `base` dbt target's artefacts land — the second
# state Recce diffs against. The pattern is separate because `**/target/` does
# not match it.
**/target-*/
# `target-base/` used to carry two exceptions — manifest.json and catalog.json —
# so a baseline travelled with the branch. It travels through the artefact store
# now, so the exceptions are gone and the whole directory is ignored like every
# other build output.
**/logs/
**/dbt_packages/
**/.duckdb-skills/
**/kg/*.duckdb
**/kg/*.duckdb.wal
**/kg/context_card.md
**/kg/atlas.html
**/kg/atlas.prev.html
**/data/*.duckdb
**/data/*.duckdb.wal

# Recce's recorded reviews and captured baselines, for every project.
#
# These were committed on purpose and the reasoning held for a while: a reviewer
# on another machine cannot reproduce a summary's numbers without the baseline
# they were measured against, and a CI runner has code and no warehouse. So they
# were inputs, not output, and worth ~1.4 MB each.
#
# It stopped holding at jaffle-shop, whose 996 marts make the same files 30 MB —
# larger than this repository's entire history — rewritten whole on every review
# run. gate.yaml anticipated exactly this: "If that becomes the dominant noise in
# reviews, the fix is to drop these four lines and untrack them."
#
# Ignoring them alone would have been the other half of a bad trade, since CI and
# the control plane both read these files. They now live in the artefact store
# (docs/ARTIFACTS.md): the producer pushes, every consumer pulls, and a 20 MB
# file never passes through a diff. `pf tool recce ci` fetches the baseline for
# the PR's base branch and publishes the review back under the head branch.
#
# Untracked by `pf artifacts migrate --apply`, which pushes and verifies every
# key before it removes anything.
**/transform/recce_state.json
**/transform/recce_summary.md
**/transform/target-base/

# A proposal pulled from a live OpenMetadata server by `pf tool openmetadata
# pull` — what data owners changed in the catalogue that this repo does not say
# yet. Transient by nature: it reflects whatever the server held at the moment
# it was fetched, and it is regenerated on every pull.
#
# Not committed, and not because it is unimportant — it is the input to a real
# pull request. But the *output* is an edit to contracts/annotations.yaml, and
# carrying the proposal alongside would leave two files claiming to say what a
# column means, which is the exact ambiguity this tool's one-direction rule
# exists to prevent.
**/catalog/owner-edits.yaml

**/reporting/queries/metrics/
# Rendered from toolkit templates by `pf evals-gen`, the same way the graph is
# rendered by `pf kg build`. Hand-written project cases sit one level up, in
# evals/cases/, and are committed.
**/evals/cases/generated/
data/pr/
.dagster/history/
.dagster/storage/
.dagster/logs/
.dagster/schedules/

# The containerised stack's DAGSTER_HOME. Its dagster.yaml is `.dagster`'s plus
# the Postgres storage block, regenerated by `pf stack render` on every start —
# derived, not authored.
.dagster-stack/

# nginx, supervisor and the launcher, likewise regenerated on every container
# start. They carry absolute host paths — supervisord needs `directory=` to be
# real, and the mount path is whatever the host's checkout is — so a committed
# copy would be one developer's machine, wrong for everyone else and silently
# overwritten at the next start.
platform/stack/

# Secrets
**/.dlt/secrets.toml
**/secrets.toml
.dagster/.nux/


#dbt
dbt.log
*.log

#connection
connection.json

# The control-plane front end. `dist/` is `npm run build` output and node_modules
# is 200MB of dependencies; both are reproducible from package-lock.json.
**/ui/static/dist/
**/ui/web/node_modules/
